    4. Build ctrl mask: ch×cw binary mask with fill ratio 0.28-0.72, ≥1 hole
    5. Assemble output: (ch*s)×(cw*s) grid; filled ctrl cells → block tile, holes → bg tile
    6. Choose ctrl color ∈ 1-9, ≠ bg, ≠ any block color
    7. Build ctrl patch from mask using ctrl color + bg
    8. Choose input grid size H×W large enough to fit both ctrl and block with ≥1 px gap + border
    9. Place ctrl and block at random non-overlapping positions (8-conn separated, border ≥1)
    10. Verify exactly 2 fg components under 8-connectivity
    11. Oracle: main(input) == output
